-- TRIGGER FUNCTION universe.set_entity_type()
-- Purpose: Automatically stamps type_id on the parent entity row when a version
--   row is first inserted. Prevents mislabelling by importers or users.
-- Accepts: TG_ARGV[0] = the slug of the entity type to look up (e.g. 'person')
-- Behaviour:
--   1. Look up the entity_type row where slug = TG_ARGV[0]. Raise exception if not found.
--   2. Read the current type_id from the parent entity row (public_entity or org_entity).
--   3. If type_id IS NULL: set it to the looked-up entity_type.id.
--   4. If type_id IS NOT NULL and matches: do nothing, allow insert.
--   5. If type_id IS NOT NULL and does NOT match: RAISE EXCEPTION — entity already
--      typed as a different type. Insert is rejected.
-- Used by: BEFORE INSERT triggers on public_person, public_organization, public_location,
--          org_person, org_organization, org_location.
-- Note: The trigger function must determine whether to update public_entity or org_entity
--   based on which version table fired it. Use TG_TABLE_NAME to branch:
--   tables prefixed 'public_' update universe.public_entity;
--   tables prefixed 'org_' update universe.org_entity.

-- TRIGGER FUNCTION universe.update_coordinates()
-- Purpose: Automatically populates the coordinates geometry column from address data
--   is NOT applicable here — coordinates must be provided explicitly by the importer
--   or geocoding pipeline. This function is NOT needed; coordinates are set directly.
-- Note: If a geocoding pipeline is added in future it should update via a new version
--   row, not by mutating an existing one.

-- SEED universe.relationship_type
